// Solution-style root: no files of its own. `tsc -b` (npm run typecheck)
// checks both projects; editors resolve each file to the project that
// includes it.
//
// Two projects because the code runs in two environments. App code runs in
// the browser and must not see Node's globals (with @types/node loaded,
// `setTimeout` returns NodeJS.Timeout and `process` type-checks, both
// wrong for the browser). Build tooling and the few tests that read files
// off disk run in Node and need `node:*` types.
{
  "files": [],
  "references": [{ "path": "./tsconfig.app.json" }, { "path": "./tsconfig.node.json" }]
}
